<p>China’s leader Xi Jinping told delegates from the People’s Liberation Army and the People’s Armed Police that the military must show political loyalty to the ruling Communist Party and keep pushing its anti-corruption campaign, as Beijing tightens discipline and oversight inside the armed forces. His remarks come after a run of dismissals and investigations involving senior officers, and at a moment when Beijing is especially wary of foreign intelligence efforts to recruit sources inside the PLA. Supporters cast the campaign as a way to boost integrity and readiness, while Xi’s stress on party loyalty highlights how closely military command remains tied to political control.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/mccLRzZpHutbd8olaWOCkkBCda6OTIQ4j0XyRhJiXuUUPHaDnVosBLLtez7ldzaKE9TJRng6ELKX8iZSrSKSjrnWWfWMHi8NBcqwG65cXtRjZ95vInBhYdKCuZljulix-P0hzFxwTXLxJIrF4-jAGIkFyits68IIVfQ1CNDOI6HM87q11a978V0sOp2yLjquQNOomtin2R0' alt='China’s President Xi Jinping at a major political gathering, as reports describe a widening military anti-graft campaign.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Oversight focus: Xi called for tougher supervision of “key areas such as fund flows, the exercise of power, and quality control” as China plans its next five-year period.</li><li>Scope and targets: RT said the post-2023 anti-graft push has led to the dismissal of multiple Central Military Commission members and dozens of generals, and that the party expelled two former defense ministers in 2023.</li><li>New investigation: RT reported an anti-graft probe into Central Military Commission vice chairman Zhang Youxia on suspicion of “serious violation of discipline and law”.</li><li>Espionage backdrop: RT said the CIA released Chinese-language recruitment ads aimed at PLA personnel; China’s Foreign Ministry condemned the effort and vowed to fight “infiltration and sabotage”.</li><li>Xi’s phrasing: Speaking to PLA and People’s Armed Police delegates, Xi said there should be “no place in the military for those who are disloyal to the party” and “no place for corrupt elements”.</li></ul><blockquote>There must be no one in the military who harbors disloyalty to the (ruling Communist) Party, - Xi Jinping</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Xi Jinping: Xi told the armed forces to stay politically loyal and keep pushing anti-corruption work, with a special focus on tighter scrutiny of money flows and the use of power. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/634126-xi-continue-corruption-purge/'>RT</a>)</li><li>China’s Foreign Ministry: The ministry condemned CIA recruitment ads aimed at PLA personnel and said China would fight “infiltration and sabotage activities” by “foreign anti-China forces”. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/634126-xi-continue-corruption-purge/'>RT</a>)</li><li>State media framing: State reporting stressed “enhancing political loyalty” and making use of the military’s “unique strengths” as the anti-graft effort expands. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/chinas-president-calls-for-political-loyalty-among-military-as-anti-graft-purge-widens/article70716800.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/634126-xi-continue-corruption-purge/'>Xi sends warning to ‘corrupt elements’ in Chinese army</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/chinas-president-calls-for-political-loyalty-among-military-as-anti-graft-purge-widens/article70716800.ece'>China’s President calls for political loyalty among military as anti-graft purge widens</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/china-xi-jinping-political-loyalty-anti-corruption-probe/'>China&#x27;s Xi Jinping calls for political loyalty amid military purge</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/xi-jinping-calls-for-absolute-military-loyalty-as-china-widens-anti-corruption-purge-13987216.html'>Xi Jinping calls for absolute military loyalty as China widens anti-corruption purge</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/chinas-xi-calls-political-loyalty-military-anti-corruption-130854096'>China’s Xi calls for political loyalty in the military as purge widens</a> - abcnews.com</li></ul>